# Entitlements map for scripts/macos_sign_notarize.sh sign-tree --entitlements-map.
# One '<glob> <plist>' pair per line. <glob> matches the path relative to the
# tree being signed; <plist> is relative to this file.
# Anything not listed is signed with NO entitlements (hardened runtime only).
#
# plugin-host = DisplayXR-owned executables that load the runtime's vendor
# plug-ins (other Team IDs). The runtime dylib itself needs nothing: library
# validation inside a third-party host app is that app's choice, not ours.
*bin/displayxr-service                  plugin-host.entitlements
# camera-host = plugin-host + the camera: the tracking host and the CLI run a
# camera-based tracking provider in-process.
*bin/displayxr-cli                      camera-host.entitlements
*bin/displayxr-tracking-host            camera-host.entitlements
# Test app inside DisplayXRCube.app: runs the runtime in-process, so a vendor
# DP plug-in loads into IT. (The bundle's CFBundleExecutable is a shell
# launcher; the real Mach-O lives in Resources/.)
Contents/Resources/cube_*               plugin-host.entitlements
